{ The second trap is the Fishing Pole Trap. The Fishing Pole is a trap most common in the Ruy Lopez (especially in the Berlin Defence and Exchange Variations). }
1. e4 { Play e5. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Ge7e5] } 1... e5 2. Nf3 { Play Nc6. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gb8c6] } 2... Nc6 3. Bb5 { This is the Ruy Lopez Opening. Now, the Fishing Pole Traps works with the Ruy Lopez Exchange Variation, and the Berlin Defense. We will be looking at this trap from both variations. Play a6 and we'll look at the Exchange Variation first! } { [%cal Ga7a6] } 3... a6 { This is called the Morphy Defence. White can play Ba4, but if he plays- } 4. Bxc6 { Bxc6, then it becomes the Exchange Variation. We take it with the d pawn. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gd7c6] } 4... dxc6 5. O-O { White castles. Remember that the Fishing Pole Trap only works if White has castled. Play Bg4 and let's jump into the trap! } { [%csl Gg4][%cal Gc8g4] } 5... Bg4 6. h3 { White plays h3. Black would have to go back or...? } 6... h5!! { No! Black doesn't have to go back! Instead, we sacrifice, THE BISHOP!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! And now, White would be fine with something like d3, BUT if white takes- } 7. hxg4?? { This is a TERRIBLE BLUNDER! Take the pawn! } { [%csl Gg4][%cal Gh5g4] } 7... hxg4 { Now, White's best move is Re1, and then we just take the Knight and White's Kingside is demolished! BUT, if white tries to defend its Knight ANYWHERE, for example- } 8. Nxe5 { Nxe5. Then, it's a forced mate in 4!! How? } { [%csl Gd8] } 8... Qh4 { Yes! We bring the queen! } 9. f4 { White plays f4. Now we lock the White king } { [%csl Gg3][%cal Gg4g3] } 9... g3 { And there's a forced mate! } { [%csl Gh1][%cal Gh4h1] } 10. Qh5 { Just take! } { [%csl Gh5][%cal Gh8h5] } 10... Rxh5 11. a3 { And mate! } { [%csl Gh1][%cal Gh4h1] } 11... Qh1# { Checkmate! } (11... Qh2# { Also fine! }) *

