{ The eighth and the last trap is called the Noah's Ark trap. It also arises from the Ruy Lopez! }
1. e4 { Play e5! } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Ge7e5] } 1... e5 2. Nf3 { Play Nc6! } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gb8c6] } 2... Nc6 3. Bb5 { Play a6! } 3... a6 4. Ba4 { And now, in the Fishing Pole, we played Nf6 and also the Exchange Variation, but now, we're gonna play d6! } { [%csl Gd6][%cal Gd7d6] } 4... d6 5. d4 { We played d6, so, White would most probably try to get the centre by d4, which is practically right! Play b5! } { [%csl Gb5][%cal Gb7b5] } 5... b5 6. Bb3 { Now we take with the Knight, setting the trap! } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc6d4] } 6... Nxd4 7. Nxd4 { And now we take back! } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Ge5d4] } 7... exd4 { White shouldn't take back here, but most of the time, white would just randomly recapture without thinking of anything! } 8. Qxd4?? { BOOM! White has fallen into our trap! What will you play here? } 8... c5 { Yes! c5! Attacking the Queen! } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc5d4] } 9. Qd5 { Now we play Be6 to defend mate and our rook! } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Gc8e6] } 9... Be6 10. Qc6+ { They give us a check! But no problem because we play Bd7! } { [%csl Gd7][%cal Ge6d7] } 10... Bd7 11. Qd5 { And now they go back! BUT THIS TIME- } 11... c4! { Yes! We don't play Be6 again! But instead, we trap White's Bishop! Black wins!! } *
